445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 132 0 R
/T (Complexity is hidden behind clean, simple interfaces. High-level components interact with abstractions rather than concrete implementations, enabling internal complexity to grow without affecting consumers. The RuleEngine calls evaluator.evaluate\(condition, eventPayload\) and receives a boolean. It has no awareness of whether the evaluation uses a strategy map, switch-case, or any other mechanism internally. This abstraction boundary means the evaluation logic can be completely replaced without touching the engine's orchestration code. 6.3 Inheritance & Polymorphism The Action Command hierarchy uses polymorphism extensively. All concrete action classes extend a common BaseAction abstract class, allowing the RuleEngine to call execute\(event, rule\) uniformly regardless of which specific action type is being executed at runtime.)
/E (Complexity is hidden behind clean, simple interfaces. High-level components interact with abstractions rather than concrete implementations, enabling internal complexity to grow without affecting consumers. The RuleEngine calls evaluator.evaluate\(condition, eventPayload\) and receives a boolean. It has no awareness of whether the evaluation uses a strategy map, switch-case, or any other mechanism internally. This abstraction boundary means the evaluation logic can be completely replaced without touching the engine's orchestration code. 6.3 Inheritance & Polymorphism The Action Command hierarchy uses polymorphism extensively. All concrete action classes extend a common BaseAction abstract class, allowing the RuleEngine to call execute\(event, rule\) uniformly regardless of which specific action type is being executed at runtime.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
