/T (The Smart HR Event-Driven Intelligent Workflow Automation Engine represents a well-architected, full-stack solution to the real-world problem of manual, rule-based HR decision-making. Its technical depth is evidenced by the deliberate application of OOP principles, SOLID design guidelines, and six proven Gang of Four design patterns across a modern TypeScript codebase.)
/E (The Smart HR Event-Driven Intelligent Workflow Automation Engine represents a well-architected, full-stack solution to the real-world problem of manual, rule-based HR decision-making. Its technical depth is evidenced by the deliberate application of OOP principles, SOLID design guidelines, and six proven Gang of Four design patterns across a modern TypeScript codebase.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
908 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 147 0 R
/T (The Observer Pattern via the EventBus brings clean, decoupled event distribution across all domain modules. The Singleton Pattern ensures resource-efficient access to the RuleEngine, EventBus, and database client. The Strategy Pattern in the Evaluator enables flexible, runtime-configurable condition evaluation without any switch-case proliferation. The Factory Method Pattern in the ActionFactory allows new action types to be added without modifying any orchestration code. The Command Pattern through BaseAction provides a uniform execution interface across all action implementations. The Repository Pattern abstracts all database queries from the engine's orchestration logic.)
/E (The Observer Pattern via the EventBus brings clean, decoupled event distribution across all domain modules. The Singleton Pattern ensures resource-efficient access to the RuleEngine, EventBus, and database client. The Strategy Pattern in the Evaluator enables flexible, runtime-configurable condition evaluation without any switch-case proliferation. The Factory Method Pattern in the ActionFactory allows new action types to be added without modifying any orchestration code. The Command Pattern through BaseAction provides a uniform execution interface across all action implementations. The Repository Pattern abstracts all database queries from the engine's orchestration logic.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
